  "tour": {
    "title": "From Garden to Garden",
    "intro": "This tour follows the Bible’s garden-shaped story: life with God in Eden, exile from that life, Jesus’ testing and victory in a garden, and the risen Christ mistaken for a gardener. It ends not with a return to a lost past, but with the Bible’s vision of creation renewed as a garden-city where God dwells with humanity.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:back-to-the-tree-of-life",
        "startSec": 154,
        "endSec": 384,
        "why": "Begin with the garden as sacred presence, not merely scenery. The speakers connect “the tree of life” with God’s presence in the temple and explain that humanity’s exile creates the longing to “get back to the tree of life,” while the promised seed will open the way through sacrifice.",
        "episodeTitle": "Back to the Tree of Life",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/0b7290bf-a0c7-4e5d-82fd-7ccd232e4385/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=0b7290bf-a0c7-4e5d-82fd-7ccd232e4385",
        "durationSec": 3141,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:why-is-there-wilderness-imagery-in-the-lords-prayer",
        "startSec": 2823,
        "endSec": 3070,
        "why": "This places Jesus in Gethsemane—the garden at the far end of the story’s crisis. The speakers call it “the opposite of the wilderness” and trace Jesus’ repeated prayer, “not what I desire, but what you desire,” back through the wilderness testing and the garden’s language of desire.",
        "episodeTitle": "The Wilderness Q+R: Why Is There Wilderness Imagery in the Lord’s Prayer?",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/9acb1e83-f4bd-4e34-ad96-82ae159bf943/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=9acb1e83-f4bd-4e34-ad96-82ae159bf943",
        "durationSec": 3755,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:trees-ancients",
        "startSec": 699,
        "endSec": 927,
        "why": "Now hear the resurrection as the fulfillment of the human vocation left unfinished in Eden. The speakers say the second Adam, “Jesus, crucified and risen,” secures what the first Adam did not attain: access to God’s eternal life and “a humanity fully in tune with God,” transformed in resurrection.",
        "episodeTitle": "Trees of the Ancients",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/57b34286-d0c1-4537-ad4b-ab151e0ac280/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=57b34286-d0c1-4537-ad4b-ab151e0ac280",
        "durationSec": 3488,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "listeners-commentary:podcast:d2454984-com-96e88155-08af-3240-94ab-4e13ecb0d2e9",
        "startSec": 583,
        "endSec": 690,
        "why": "This is the intimate hinge of the tour: in John 20, Mary sees the risen Jesus but thinks “he was the gardener.” The commentator follows her grief, her recognition when Jesus says “Mary,” and her commission to announce, “I have seen the Lord.”",
        "episodeTitle": "John 20:1-31",
        "sourceId": "listeners-commentary",
        "source": "The Listener's Commentary",
        "audioUrl": "https://mcdn.podbean.com/mf/web/z8yyjpv9fmtit6hd/john_201-3185o5y.mp3",
        "durationSec": 1726,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:heavenly-city",
        "startSec": 3190,
        "endSec": 3325,
        "why": "Finish with the destination: not simply Eden restored, but garden, city, temple, and new creation gathered together. The speakers describe “the tent of God” dwelling among humans, open gates, a river and trees, and the tree of life flowing from God’s throne—“an infinite source of abundance and life.”",
        "episodeTitle": "The City E13: The Heavenly City",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/fc7f7a97-7350-4315-8216-76eb3af655a5/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=fc7f7a97-7350-4315-8216-76eb3af655a5",
        "durationSec": 3918,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      }
    ],
    "closing": "Taken together, these clips move from guarded access to the tree of life, through Jesus’ faithful surrender in the garden and his resurrection appearance, toward a future where the garden is no longer closed. The final image is God’s presence filling the whole renewed world: life flowing outward, and humanity finally at home with God.",
